  // Signatures: the ability that makes this Warrior different from that one.
  //
  // A character is a CLASS (its basic and how fast it gains health), a SIGNATURE (one of these)
  // and an AFFINITY (what the signature is made of). The class is what everyone of that kind can
  // do; the signature and affinity are the roll the Tavern is worth hunting through.
  // Design doc 05 §1.
  //
  // An affinity is NOT a separate ability per combination: the signature's ability is retuned to
  // the rolled affinity, which keeps its total damage and changes its damage type - and therefore
  // which status effect it applies. AffinityAbilities is the sparse exception for a signature whose
  // affinities really are different spells; the mage's Blast is a different explosion for each.
  //
  // AllowedAffinities empty means all eight. The mage signatures list seven, because a bolt of
  // Physical is not a thing.
  //
  // AWAKENING is what the signature grows into. Stage is derived from RARITY (the ceiling:
  // Common II, Rare III, Epic IV, Legendary Apex) and LEVEL (the climb: II at 10, III at 20,
  // IV and Apex at 30) - never stored, so a save cannot claim a stage it has not earned.
  // Stages are CUMULATIVE: II is still there under IV. Stage I is the signature itself and has
  // no entry. Stages II and IV are the same for every signature (potency, then a spike); III and
  // Apex are its own, which is where two level-30 characters stop feeling like one character.
  // Design doc 05 §2.
